1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:01,918
<i>Ma…</i>

2
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:04,087
<i>Please, don't do that again.</i>

3
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:06,923
<i>Remember what I told you? I'll find a way.</i>

4
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:11,636
<i>I can't bear to see you suffer, my dear.</i>

5
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:13,012
<i>I'm not suffering.</i>

6
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:14,723
<i>I never said that I was suffering.</i>

7
00:00:14,806 --> 00:00:17,434
<i>I promise you.</i>
<i>I'll get back at Billy.</i>

8
00:00:17,517 --> 00:00:19,060
[BILLY] <i>They may be delusional.</i>

9
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:22,272
<i>They believe in their own version</i>
<i>of the truth.</i>

10
00:00:22,355 --> 00:00:24,315
<i>But that still doesn't change the fact</i>

11
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:27,360
<i>Bea has to pay for what she did.</i>

12
00:00:28,695 --> 00:00:33,033
<i>Wish me luck actually</i>
<i>falling asleep tonight.</i>

13
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:34,743
[JORDAN] <i>You want to fall asleep?</i>

14
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:39,122
<i>♪ My muse ♪</i>

15
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:43,001
<i>♪ Where's our destination? ♪</i>

16
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:47,839
<i>♪ You are the captain ♪</i>

17
00:00:47,922 --> 00:00:52,635
<i>♪ I'll follow wherever you go ♪</i>

18
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:54,471
<i>- It's beautiful.</i>
<i>- ♪ Oh, baby ♪</i>

19
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:58,892
<i>♪ I'll ride your wave ♪</i>

20
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:03,104
<i>♪ Wherever it takes me ♪</i>

21
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:07,442
<i>♪ My heart won't be lost ♪</i>

22
00:01:07,525 --> 00:01:12,030
<i>♪ Even if you let go, I'll come back ♪</i>

23
00:01:13,364 --> 00:01:15,742
[HUMMING]

24
00:01:17,452 --> 00:01:20,789
<i>♪ Stay right there, my love ♪</i>

25
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:22,832
<i>♪ I'm coming home ♪</i>

26
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:25,001
[ABRUPT, UNSETTLING MUSIC]

27
00:01:25,084 --> 00:01:26,461
[GASPS]

28
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:27,504
[BILLY] <i>Hello, dude?</i>

29
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:29,130
<i>Could you come with me?</i>

30
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:34,260
<i>Miss, is there really no way we can look</i>
<i>at Mariela Mercado's files?</i>

31
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:37,305
[HEAD NURSE]
<i>I'm really sorry, ma'am, but you can't.</i>

32
00:01:37,388 --> 00:01:38,848
<i>Those are confidential.</i>

33
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:40,725
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

34
00:01:47,398 --> 00:01:50,610
[BILLY] <i>And fuel prices have</i>
<i>increased again! My gosh!</i>

35
00:01:50,693 --> 00:01:53,488
<i>Even electricity!</i>
<i>Everything's getting pricier!</i>

36
00:01:53,571 --> 00:01:56,533
<i>- That's why we have to go.</i>
- [NURSE] <i>Is that so?</i>

37
00:01:56,616 --> 00:01:57,992
[BILLY] <i>We might get caught in the rain.</i>

38
00:01:58,076 --> 00:01:59,744
<i>- I'm sorry for the trouble.</i>
- [NURSE] <i>It's fine.</i>

39
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:00,954
[BILLY] <i>Take care!</i>

40
00:02:01,037 --> 00:02:03,289
<i>Do you know what caused the fire?</i>

41
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:05,416
[CLERK] <i>No one knows, miss.</i>

42
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,586
<i>All I heard was that Mariela survived.</i>

43
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:10,380
<i>And so did her youngest daughter.</i>

44
00:02:10,463 --> 00:02:12,757
<i>But her eldest daughter died.</i>

45
00:02:12,841 --> 00:02:14,509
[JORDAN] <i>When did the fire happen?</i>

46
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:18,221
[CLERK] <i>About 12 or 13 years ago, I think.</i>

47
00:02:18,304 --> 00:02:20,807
[BILLY] <i>But the father</i>
<i>wasn't with them?</i>

48
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:22,600
[CLERK]
<i>No, he wasn't.</i>

49
00:02:22,684 --> 00:02:26,271
<i>The rumor is that</i>
<i>Mariela's husband left her.</i>

50
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:35,655
[JORDAN GRUNTS]

51
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:38,616
[JORDAN EXHALES SHARPLY]

52
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,660
It turns out Bea went through a lot.

53
00:02:41,786 --> 00:02:43,997
But our question remains unanswered.

54
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,832
What's your connection to this?

55
00:02:46,457 --> 00:02:48,710
She lied about her sister.

56
00:02:48,793 --> 00:02:51,129
But what she said about her father?

57
00:02:51,212 --> 00:02:52,463
That seems to be true.

58
00:02:53,464 --> 00:02:55,508
Well, if her father is still alive,

59
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:57,927
maybe we can get answers from him.

60
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:03,182
Yes, of course. I will help you find him.

61
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:10,064
Someone caused trouble
at your house last night?

62
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:13,902
Yes. The mother of the woman
who's mad at Billy.

63
00:03:13,985 --> 00:03:15,653
Why is she mad at Billy?

64
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:17,113
No idea.

65
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:19,532
Maybe because of envy.

66
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:22,744
I don't know why she hates Billy so much,

67
00:03:22,827 --> 00:03:26,122
to the point that she even
conspired with a criminal.

68
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:27,916
A criminal?

69
00:03:27,999 --> 00:03:28,833
[PRECIOUS] Yes.

70
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:31,920
Remember when I told you
someone broke into our house?

71
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:34,047
Apparently, he had a different motive.

72
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:36,424
He wanted to scare us. Especially Billy.

73
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:40,094
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [SPRAY PAINT CAN HISSING]

74
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:41,846
- [BILLY GRUNTS]
- [BODY THUDS]

75
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:47,018
[INHALES SHARPLY]
<i>Hurry up. Hurry up. Hurry up.</i>

76
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:49,270
[GRUNTS]

77
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:52,357
<i>- Give up already!</i>
<i>- Help! Let me go!</i>

78
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:54,025
[BILLY GRUNTING]

79
00:03:54,108 --> 00:03:56,194
<i>- Stop resisting!</i>
- [GRUNTS]

80
00:03:56,277 --> 00:03:58,947
<i>Auntie Pres! Help!</i>

81
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,951
<i>Auntie, was that Billy?</i>

82
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:05,703
<i>My God, Billy!</i>

83
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:06,871
<i>Billy!</i>

84
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:07,789
<i>Billy?</i>

85
00:04:07,872 --> 00:04:10,041
<i>Help! Please help us!</i>

86
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:11,501
<i>Billy?</i>

87
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:14,087
<i>My God, Billy, what happened?</i>

88
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:16,923
[PANICKED BREATHING]
<i>Billy. Billy. Billy.</i>

89
00:04:17,006 --> 00:04:18,549
<i>Help!</i>

90
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:20,677
<i>Please help us!</i>

91
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:22,804
<i>Billy? Billy. Billy. Billy.</i>

92
00:04:22,887 --> 00:04:24,055
<i>My God!</i>

93
00:04:24,138 --> 00:04:25,181
<i>Jordan!</i>

94
00:04:26,015 --> 00:04:28,393
<i>- Jordan, help me!</i>
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

95
00:04:28,476 --> 00:04:30,103
<i>- Auntie Pres!</i>
<i>- Billy?</i>

96
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:32,105
<i>- What happened to Billy?</i>
<i>- Watch her for a second.</i>

97
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:33,815
<i>I'll call an ambulance.</i>

98
00:04:33,898 --> 00:04:34,732
<i>Dude.</i>

99
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:35,984
What?!

100
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:37,527
Yes, that happened.

101
00:04:38,236 --> 00:04:42,573
Well, authorities are now
hunting down that guy,

102
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:44,784
and the mother has been given a warning.

103
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:47,328
So, I hope things will be okay now.

104
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:49,497
Are things really okay?

105
00:04:50,123 --> 00:04:50,957
I hope so.

106
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:53,584
Your son is in a fight.

107
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:54,877
- What?!
- What?!

108
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,422
Where's Oliver?

109
00:04:58,089 --> 00:04:59,299
He's over there.

110
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:08,516
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:05:45,636 --> 00:05:47,638
[OLIVER] You think I won't fight you?

112
00:05:47,722 --> 00:05:49,390
Let's see who's tough.

113
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,225
You might just end up crying.

114
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:52,727
You're such a mama's boy.

115
00:05:53,352 --> 00:05:55,354
- Oh, I mean an auntie's boy.
- [BOY 1] Ooh!

116
00:05:55,938 --> 00:05:57,190
She's not your mom, right?

117
00:05:57,273 --> 00:05:59,275
What did you say, huh? Say that again.

118
00:05:59,358 --> 00:06:00,651
- You can't do it.
- Say it. I dare you.

119
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:01,986
- Oliver!
- Come on!

120
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:04,530
- I can fight you, you know?
- Hey! Oliver!

121
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:06,074
Break it up!

122
00:06:06,157 --> 00:06:07,867
Go back to your classroom.

123
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:10,787
What are you all looking at?

124
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:12,330
Go back to your classrooms.

125
00:06:13,831 --> 00:06:15,792
Oliver, what happened?

126
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:17,794
He called me an auntie's boy.

127
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:19,337
It was embarrassing.

128
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:22,256
Why are you mad about that?

129
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,467
It's true that you're your
auntie's boy, isn't it?

130
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:26,803
Your Aunt Precious loves you so much.

131
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:28,596
There's nothing embarrassing about that.

132
00:06:28,679 --> 00:06:31,307
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

133
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:32,558
You're right, Sir Eric.

134
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:34,102
I'm sorry.

135
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:35,436
Auntie, I love you.

136
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,564
- I'm sorry. I love you.
- Love you.

137
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:41,859
It's a good thing you were both here.

138
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:44,320
I'll go now.

139
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:46,781
- Thank you.
- Okay, go now.

140
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:55,206
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

141
00:06:57,542 --> 00:06:59,877
I understand where my mom is coming from.

142
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:01,838
Of course she wanted to confront them.

143
00:07:01,921 --> 00:07:03,339
But unfortunately,

144
00:07:04,507 --> 00:07:06,968
it made the problem worse.

145
00:07:07,635 --> 00:07:09,595
Why don't you just tell her the truth?

146
00:07:10,596 --> 00:07:12,306
Are you out of your mind?

147
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:13,683
You want me to tell her the truth?

148
00:07:15,726 --> 00:07:18,813
There are only two possible outcomes
if she finds out who Billy is.

149
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:21,274
Either she kills someone,

150
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:24,360
or she tries to kill herself again.

151
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:27,613
I don't want that to happen to Mama.

152
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:31,909
How long are you going to keep it hidden?

153
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:34,078
She's going to find out
the truth eventually.

154
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:37,874
If she finds out the truth,

155
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:39,876
Billy's done for.

156
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:43,379
I'll make her suffer
while I'm enjoying a good life.

157
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:45,631
That way, Mama won't have
to worry about anything.

158
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:47,842
But how can I do that?

159
00:07:48,676 --> 00:07:51,471
I keep losing against her.

160
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:55,933
I don't even have money
to pay the electricity bill or our rent.

161
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:58,436
Plus, I'm being linked to your case.

162
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:07,570
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

163
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:09,864
Here.

164
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:13,034
What's this?

165
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:15,328
[BEA] This…?

166
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:18,080
Hey.

167
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:19,373
- What?
- Where did you get this?

168
00:08:19,457 --> 00:08:20,875
From my part-time job.

169
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:24,295
- You stole this, didn't you?
- Of course not.

170
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:29,258
- I can't accept this.
- That's yours.

171
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,635
Take it.

172
00:08:30,718 --> 00:08:32,512
I have nothing to lose anyway.

173
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:34,013
Except you.

174
00:08:36,098 --> 00:08:37,016
All right then.

175
00:08:37,683 --> 00:08:39,060
- [GRUNTS]
- [SOFT THUD]

176
00:08:39,143 --> 00:08:40,311
That's so cheesy.

177
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:42,104
[CALOY CHUCKLES]

178
00:08:44,315 --> 00:08:45,566
All right.

179
00:08:49,111 --> 00:08:55,117
[MUSIC BECOMES STIRRING]

180
00:08:56,994 --> 00:08:57,995
'Bi.

181
00:09:02,291 --> 00:09:03,167
What?

182
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:04,794
There's something I need you to do.

183
00:09:11,717 --> 00:09:12,677
[JORDAN] No trace.

184
00:09:14,637 --> 00:09:16,556
It seems they erased everything.

185
00:09:17,765 --> 00:09:19,350
Are they hiding from someone?

186
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:21,394
So, what does that mean?

187
00:09:21,477 --> 00:09:23,062
They're a family of criminals?

188
00:09:23,771 --> 00:09:26,399
Well, Caloy is a hacking expert.

189
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:29,527
He probably erased all info
about Bea's dad.

190
00:09:32,029 --> 00:09:33,114
Don't worry.

191
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:34,865
I have to find something.

192
00:09:37,743 --> 00:09:39,161
"Mercado."

193
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:41,247
Sorry for the hassle.

194
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:43,583
You got dragged into my problems again.

195
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:45,084
Your problems?

196
00:09:45,751 --> 00:09:47,295
Dude, what are you even saying?

197
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:49,463
I'm doing this for you.

198
00:09:50,798 --> 00:09:52,592
- [SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]
- And LoveList.

199
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:54,719
If you go down, we all go down.

200
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:58,514
Am I going to let that happen?
Of course not.

201
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:01,434
Thank you.

202
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:08,733
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

203
00:10:08,816 --> 00:10:09,900
[JORDAN] Okay.

204
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:20,953
Ms. Talia? Ms. Talia!

205
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:22,788
- Yes?
- Ms. Talia, hi.

206
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:24,915
- Do you remember me?
- Uh…

207
00:10:24,999 --> 00:10:27,043
- I'm sorry--
- I applied to your company.

208
00:10:27,126 --> 00:10:29,795
- Bea. Bea Mercado.
- Oh. Oh, right!

209
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:31,130
Yes, um…

210
00:10:31,213 --> 00:10:32,673
Ms. Talia, uh…

211
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:34,550
I hope you can hear me out.

212
00:10:35,134 --> 00:10:40,014
You see, my mother is sick,
so I really need a job.

213
00:10:40,097 --> 00:10:45,895
I know there's a high chance
that you won't hire me.

214
00:10:45,978 --> 00:10:47,772
That's why I'm here.

215
00:10:47,855 --> 00:10:52,109
I came to talk to you directly
to hopefully convince you.

216
00:10:52,193 --> 00:10:54,820
- I know that the reason--
- [MOTORCYCLE ENGINE ROARING]

217
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:56,822
- Hey! Hey!
- [TALIA GASPS]

218
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:58,032
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE ROARING]

219
00:10:58,115 --> 00:10:59,617
[TALIA] Oh! Oh my God!

220
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:01,410
[GASPS] Are you okay?

221
00:11:01,494 --> 00:11:02,870
Oh my goodness!

222
00:11:02,953 --> 00:11:04,497
- Oh…
- [BEA GRUNTS]

223
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:06,165
You're wounded!

224
00:11:06,248 --> 00:11:07,833
[SOFT GROAN] I'm okay, ma'am.

225
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:10,878
- Are you okay?
- Yes. Here's your bag.

226
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:13,005
Bea, right?

227
00:11:13,964 --> 00:11:14,882
Yes, ma'am.

228
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:17,093
Thank you so much.

229
00:11:17,176 --> 00:11:23,891
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:11:25,017 --> 00:11:28,104
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

231
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:34,860
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

232
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:41,867
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

233
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:56,590
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

234
00:11:59,385 --> 00:12:00,928
<i>Look at this kid.</i>

235
00:12:01,011 --> 00:12:02,263
[JUDE, YOUNG JORDAN CHUCKLING]

236
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:06,684
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

237
00:12:08,894 --> 00:12:09,895
<i>Jade?</i>

238
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:12,815
<i>Jade!</i>

239
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:14,024
<i>Mommy!</i>

240
00:12:14,108 --> 00:12:15,067
<i>Mommy!</i>

241
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:17,445
[VOICE SHAKING] <i>Mommy!</i>

242
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:21,866
[SOBS] Mommy!

243
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:33,043
[PAPERS RUSTLING]

244
00:12:38,632 --> 00:12:45,598
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:15,753
[MUSIC FADES]

246
00:13:16,295 --> 00:13:18,714
[HEELS CLACKING]

247
00:13:18,797 --> 00:13:21,050
- [BEA] Oh! Hi!
- [HR OFFICER] Hi.

248
00:13:21,133 --> 00:13:23,511
You didn't call me.

249
00:13:23,594 --> 00:13:24,929
Never mind, that's okay.

250
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:31,769
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

251
00:13:33,562 --> 00:13:37,358
[CELLPHONE RINGING]

252
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:40,236
Hello, Ma?

253
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:43,572
Perhaps I should find a job.

254
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:48,619
I'm your mother. Of the two of us,
I should be the one working.

255
00:13:48,702 --> 00:13:51,080
Why do you want to work all of a sudden?

256
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:52,331
It's fine, Ma.

257
00:13:52,414 --> 00:13:56,168
When Papa left us, you and Abi
worked yourselves to the bone

258
00:13:56,252 --> 00:13:57,545
for our family.

259
00:13:57,628 --> 00:13:59,129
Now, it's my turn.

260
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:01,382
Did you find a decent company this time?

261
00:14:01,465 --> 00:14:02,758
Yes, Ma.

262
00:14:03,384 --> 00:14:04,927
They made me a supervisor.

263
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:07,680
They did?! That's my daughter!

264
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:10,808
That Billy can't look down on you now!

265
00:14:10,891 --> 00:14:12,309
[CHUCKLES]

266
00:14:12,393 --> 00:14:14,853
Anyway, I have to go, Ma.
We're quite busy here.

267
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:15,938
Bye.

268
00:14:16,021 --> 00:14:22,945
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

269
00:14:23,612 --> 00:14:24,780
[CALOY] <i>Sorry.</i>

270
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:28,701
<i>I was too rough, so you got dragged.</i>

271
00:14:29,785 --> 00:14:32,288
<i>It's fine. It made our act</i>
<i>even more convincing.</i>

272
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:34,999
<i>Ms. Talia really felt bad for me.</i>

273
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,296
<i>- But I hurt you.</i>
<i>- Tsk!</i>

274
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:42,548
<i>I said it's okay.</i>

275
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:53,517
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

276
00:14:58,647 --> 00:15:00,816
- Bea.
- Oh! Ma'am!

277
00:15:02,109 --> 00:15:06,030
Uh, Ms. Talia, I haven't gotten
the chance to thank you.

278
00:15:08,657 --> 00:15:13,120
Thank you so much, ma'am, for hiring me

279
00:15:13,203 --> 00:15:16,081
despite the fact that
I have a police record.

280
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:18,250
I'm so grateful.

281
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:21,545
You know, I believe in second chances.

282
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:23,297
And I also believe

283
00:15:23,380 --> 00:15:25,549
that you deserve a second chance.

284
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:29,219
Thank you so much. Thank you.

285
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,764
Because of that, I'll do my best.

286
00:15:31,847 --> 00:15:34,391
That said, I should get back to work.

287
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:35,601
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

288
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:37,227
- Okay.
- Excuse me, ma'am.

289
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:44,193
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

290
00:15:45,527 --> 00:15:49,281
[NO AUDIBLE DIALOG]

291
00:15:53,243 --> 00:15:55,287
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

292
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:59,541
I promise, from here on,
it only gets better,

293
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:03,420
because every Filipina
deserves to feel safe

294
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:05,631
and empowered in love.

295
00:16:06,757 --> 00:16:07,675
Thank you.

296
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:09,510
Thank you!

297
00:16:10,094 --> 00:16:13,597
- [APPLAUSE]
- [GUSHING]

298
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:15,891
How was it? Be honest.

299
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,435
- No notes, chief.
- [BILLY] Hmm?

300
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:20,688
Yes, you delivered it so well!

301
00:16:20,771 --> 00:16:22,064
- Right?
- You're awesome!

302
00:16:22,147 --> 00:16:23,691
- [CHARM] Perfect!
- I didn't talk too fast?

303
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:25,609
- [TONI] No, you're good!
- [CHARM] You did so well!

304
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:27,361
- [MARJ] I think it's perfect.
- Guys?

305
00:16:27,444 --> 00:16:30,072
So, I have good news.

306
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:33,409
I have a potential sponsor,

307
00:16:33,492 --> 00:16:34,952
and it's…

308
00:16:37,579 --> 00:16:39,623
Talia & Co., the jewelry brand!

309
00:16:39,707 --> 00:16:40,624
[GIGGLES]

310
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:42,292
- Wow!
- Yeah!

311
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:44,628
Do you guys know how huge this is?

312
00:16:44,712 --> 00:16:46,672
I went to their showroom once,

313
00:16:46,755 --> 00:16:49,383
and their engagement rings are beautiful!

314
00:16:49,466 --> 00:16:50,509
Oh?

315
00:16:51,301 --> 00:16:54,221
You're checking out rings?
Shouldn't that be Ralph's job?

316
00:16:54,304 --> 00:16:56,724
Perhaps she was inspired by Val.

317
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:58,976
Maybe she wants to be the one to propose.

318
00:16:59,643 --> 00:17:02,229
- [AWKWARD LAUGHTER]
- Sorry, what's the tea?

319
00:17:02,312 --> 00:17:03,564
Anyway!

320
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:05,816
Do you want this sponsorship deal or not?

321
00:17:05,899 --> 00:17:10,946
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

322
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:12,448
What do you think?

323
00:17:13,323 --> 00:17:14,867
[TONI] It sounds great.

324
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:17,786
I mean, that's a good partnership.

325
00:17:19,496 --> 00:17:20,873
- Okay.
- Okay!

326
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:22,332
- Let's do it!
- [CLAPS]

327
00:17:22,416 --> 00:17:23,542
Thank you, Val.

328
00:17:24,126 --> 00:17:25,627
Good.

329
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:27,921
Because this sponsorship
is already in the bag.

330
00:17:28,005 --> 00:17:29,882
They just have one request, though.

331
00:17:29,965 --> 00:17:30,966
Okay…

332
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:34,344
They want you to wear this
to the awards night.

333
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,514
This necklace costs 30 million.

334
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:38,682
Oh.

335
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:39,975
[TONI] Gosh.

336
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:41,060
[BILLY] Wow.

337
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:42,770
[CHARM] It's beautiful!

338
00:17:42,853 --> 00:17:48,108
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

339
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,739
Our collaboration
with celebrity influencer Maxie

340
00:17:53,822 --> 00:17:55,032
was a success.

341
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:56,992
Aside from the exposure,

342
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:59,828
we experienced
increased traffic on our website

343
00:17:59,912 --> 00:18:01,163
after it was released.

344
00:18:01,663 --> 00:18:04,666
Thank you very much, Hannah,
for that presentation.

345
00:18:05,292 --> 00:18:07,878
Ever since we rolled out this campaign,

346
00:18:07,961 --> 00:18:10,255
there has been an increase in
the number of our followers.

347
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:13,092
And of course, this translates into

348
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:14,384
sales!

349
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:16,887
So we are continuing this campaign

350
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:19,473
with our next partner,

351
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:22,976
Billy Cariño of LoveList.

352
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:23,936
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

353
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:27,356
[TALIA] She is the perfect
next partner for us.

354
00:18:27,439 --> 00:18:30,359
More than just having a big following
and being a businesswoman,

355
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:32,653
she is relevant.

356
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:35,948
And the profile of LoveList members,

357
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:39,076
it has the demographics
of our target market.

358
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:41,161
Imagine!

359
00:18:42,079 --> 00:18:45,707
If she is wearing one of our power pieces,

360
00:18:45,791 --> 00:18:48,127
what a statement it will make.

361
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:52,005
What do you think?
It's a great idea, right?

362
00:18:52,631 --> 00:18:53,715
What do you think?

363
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:57,719
It's a great idea, right?

364
00:18:57,803 --> 00:19:01,140
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

365
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:02,933
<i>Like I've said before,</i>

366
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:05,602
<i>just use me.</i>

367
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:08,939
<i>Anything, everything you tell me to do,</i>
<i>I'll do it all.</i>

368
00:19:09,022 --> 00:19:10,941
<i>I'll help you.</i>

369
00:19:12,317 --> 00:19:13,527
- What do you think?
- Sounds great!

370
00:19:13,610 --> 00:19:14,611
Yes!

371
00:19:15,237 --> 00:19:16,780
Uh, Bea?

372
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:18,907
- Ma'am?
- [TALIA] Yes?

373
00:19:18,991 --> 00:19:21,535
Yes, I agree with you, Ms. Talia!

374
00:19:21,618 --> 00:19:22,995
Very good.

375
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:26,832
I think she'll make a wonderful partner
for our event.

376
00:19:26,915 --> 00:19:33,172
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

377
00:19:39,803 --> 00:19:41,805
<i>We hit the jackpot with this!</i>

378
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:44,433
<i>This will be a huge blow to Billy!</i>

379
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:46,351
<i>Just tell me when and where.</i>

380
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:47,477
<i>How does it look?</i>

381
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:48,645
[CHARM] <i>Wow, it's so pretty!</i>

382
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:50,689
<i>Definitely worth 30 million!</i>

383
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:54,401
<i>Keep your eyes on it later, okay?</i>
<i>We can't afford to lose it.</i>

384
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:58,030
- [HUMMING]
- [GUITAR STRUMMING]

385
00:19:58,113 --> 00:19:58,947
[JORDAN] <i>Sorry.</i>

386
00:19:59,031 --> 00:20:02,117
<i>When you sing,</i>
<i>you give us all the feels.</i>

387
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:04,161
<i>But why do you seem</i>
<i>so distracted today?</i>

388
00:20:04,244 --> 00:20:09,082
<i>Just imagine you're singing</i>
<i>to the love of your life.</i>

389
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:11,919
[JORDAN] <i>I searched</i>
<i>every corner of the Net.</i>

390
00:20:12,002 --> 00:20:13,003
[BILLY] <i>Mm-hmm?</i>

391
00:20:13,086 --> 00:20:15,881
<i>But I couldn't find anything</i>
<i>about Bea's dad</i>

392
00:20:15,964 --> 00:20:17,132
<i>or her family.</i>
